Ian Stirling <root@mauve.demon.co.uk> wrote:
> Take a flint stone, a unicorn horn, and high dex.
> Apply the unicorn horn to the flint stone, and if lucky, you get (randomly)
> a flint blade, a flint axehead, or a flint spearhead.

	I feel like this may have come up before.  I kind of like the idea,
having a little stone-tool-making experience myself (and the scars to
prove it).  I would suggest that you should also be able to do it using
a rock and a flint stone.  (Rocks are better for large flakes and quick
shaping, although antlers or copper points are better for fine work.)

	If you fail your roll when attempting flintcraft, I'd suggest that
you take some minor damage: "Ouch!  The sharp edge of the flint cuts
your body_part(hand) as it shatters!"  If really unlucky, perhaps you
should get a splinter in your eye, blinding you.  Also, perhaps higher
dexterity should allow you to make better objects - certainly I had my
share of experiences like 
"Hey, this spearhead is coming along nicely..."
*CRACK*  
"OK, this _arrowhead_ is coming along nicely..."

	Problems that I see are:
- Why would you ever actually use this?  Just to get an axe or a spear?
They're all over the place anyway.
- Now we have to have stone axes, stone spears, etc.  Those weapons are
assumed to be metallic in the code, and there would have to be changes
to accomodate that.  I guess we could just add new items, but there has
to be a point to it.

